  "physical_release": false,
  "scope_note": "Standard reconstruction includes full-count tracks, individual upper/main hull plates, both hollow sponson shells and engine-roof louvers. 58 lower and two HB-transferred upper roller stations are physical, with independent source picks and documented rail offsets and spring/ring conflicts. Four upper support angles, 34 lower support angles and 76 lower attachment bolts have separate occurrences. Front skirt borders now follow reviewed SNL2 points, retaining the initial trace and unreviewed middle/rear transition. Both idlers have separate rims, disks, boss, diaphragms, rivets, bushes, shafts and partial adjusting installations. Contours, drilling, threads, rear support ownership, removable retention and many hull/upper attachments remain approximate or missing. Drive wheels, remaining structure/fittings, detailed machinery and interiors remain in progress. Standard assembled geometry takes priority over poses. Both driving wheels now have source-complete shaft BOMs and partial bearing/attachment installations. Inner rear panel mapping is corrected from joint allocations; skirt border and casting geometry remain inferred. Partial source-counted roller pinion: 73 rotating leaves, four shaft-assembly leaves, two separate bushes and nineteen named mounting leaves per side. Casting profiles, counterbores, end journals, M1546 bearing, oil drilling and nominal pipe-thread envelopes are inferred. Inner Q52E plug is cut flush per HB132; outside head retained. Cotters are unsplayed supplied-length approximations; formed retention is unqualified. Static angle 17.21 degrees and explicit 1.8033 mm inward station correction clear the existing 35-tooth hypothesis at one position. Continuous gearing, 35/37 tooth conflict, detailed lubrication/sealing, threads and full shared-part quantity reconciliation remain unresolved.",
  "missing_layout_families": [
    "Detailed electrical starter/generator placement",
    "Ventilation fan and duct envelope",
    "External armament and exact sponson interfaces",
    "Control linkage routes",
    "Complete roller/suspension station solution"
  ],
